                <pb facs="0826" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/1274: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hammond</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Sebastián</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-25T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                                1926—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>62. My telegram number 60, August 25 [<hi rendition="#italic">15</hi>], 1 p.m.
                    Note just received from Foreign Office invites the United States together with
                    France, Great Britain and Italy, as well as all states adhering to <pb
                        facs="0827" n="731" xml:id="pg731"/> Tangier statute, to participate with
                    Spain in a conference at Geneva September 1st to examine Tangier question with
                    special reference to Spain’s desire for incorporation of International Zone with
                    Spanish Zone. Full text of note follows by telegraph. Repeated to London, Paris,
                    and Rome.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hammond</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
